hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan today I'm  going to answer question from one of our  readers Rita who wrote insane I'm into  network marketing and recruiting  qualified people into my team is a  problem how do I get the right people  onto my team so thanks for the question  Rita the way I look at network marketing  is similar to a franchise in business  and if you want to franchise your  business what you have to be able to do  number one is show that it can work  yourself so a lot of people get into  network marketing they don't have any  success and actually selling what all  they do is try to go out and recruit  people to join their team in the grand  scheme of things you're gonna make money  by having a profitable team who's out  there selling for you but you have to  know how to do it yourself you have to  build a model where you're out selling  making money so when you're talking to  people and trying to convince them to  come on board you can show them hey I've  done this this works and this can work  for you so number one is making sure  that you're able to sell the product  yourself you believe in it you've had  success and you can duplicate that  success by bringing other people on  board if you go on your pitching people  and you haven't had much access yourself  it's gonna be really hard to convince  him to want to sign up with you ok so  that's number one the second thing is  I'd really make sure I'm qualifying  people so you don't want to just accept  anybody into your program if you want to  have a successful network marketing  business or any business really you  really have to make sure that you're  spending the time training and  communicating with your people so  there's a lot of time investment right  you don't want to just sign somebody up  and say here you go and hopefully you  know they do well it's not really like  that if you look at the most successful  business owners and in network marketing  or any company you'll find that they've  invested into their team so it takes a  lot of time to put that work into your  team you want to make sure that you're  getting a commitment up front and not  wasting your time on somebody who's not  going to commit back to you so think  about the personality characteristics  you want to somebody working in your  business think about some qualifying  questions you can ask with some tasks  you can have them do to make sure that  they're really committed to doing this  before you go down the road or spending  a lot of time and effort with them and  they leave your business they don't have  success they drop it to do something  else so make sure you're really  qualifying upfront before we accept  somebody up onto your team you have a  lot more success with three or five  really highly motivated energetic people  who really want to make this work than  fifty people who have just signed up and  don't do anything with it right so  really focus on the quality they're over  the quantity and in the last bit advice  I have for you is make sure you stick  with them so assuming you found the  right person and you've built up a  system where you've done it yourself and  you can help people you have to train  them and mentor them starting in any  business is really hard right there's a  lot of excitement at the beginning and  that there at the start you're you're  feeding off of those fumes of excitement  and energy but then reality hits you and  you notice this is a lot harder than I  thought it was gonna be and at that  point a lot of these guys will drop off  and you don't want that to happen so you  have to show them that there is a way if  they stick with it they're gonna make  money they're gonna be successful and  you guide and mentor them along that  path so it's not just signing up new  people it's also continuing with your  existing people the ones you've put a  lot of time and effort into until  they're past their survival point once  somebody gets the system and they're  making enough money to support  themselves feed their families live  their lives then they can expand on that  success and you don't have to put as  much ongoing effort into it if they have  questions they want to mentor you have  to be there for them that's part of  being the boss being at the top but you  don't want to bend them them too early  and a lot of archers make this mistake  is they bring people on they give them a  little bit of training and say okay here  you go you've got to work with them  through those hard times especially at  the beginning and in network marketing  especially because it is tough to get  those first sales and if they don't see  some really success they're gonna get  discouraged and they're gonna quit on  you and so you've spent all this time  building up a system and recruiting and  training and you don't want people to  abandon ship because they don't have  immediate success so set them up for  success as much as you can and stick  with them through those hard times  especially at the beginning so that they  stay motivated to want to stay on your  team and continue building their own  little business so hopefully that helps  for those of you watching if you like  the video please give it a thumbs up  below it makes me want to do more of  these videos for you and I'd love to  hear you have to think about this video  if you want to leave a comment under the  under below and we have a question about  your own business feel free to ask it I  love seeing those and I try to respond  to everybody sometimes taking a little  bit but I'll try to respond as soon as I  can so thank you and you'll see you on  the next episode
 

